Wasmtime 48.0.8, Bytecode Alliance:
fh statically embeds the full Wasmtime C API, Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.
https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/releases/tag/v48.0.8
The complete license, pinned archive/source provenance, macOS arm64 dependency
notices and Rust runtime notices are retained under licenses/wasmtime/. Native library
archives are fetched for builds, not committed in this source tree. The retained
guest Wasm modules do not contain the host Wasmtime runtime.

Zig 0.16.0:
fh and its retained Zig-built Wasm modules include Zig standard-library and
compiler-runtime code. Copyright (c) Zig contributors. MIT; complete text in
licenses/zig/LICENSE.

WASI libc:
The retained C test fixture native/loops/fixtures/wasm/transform-c.wasm includes
wasi-libc as bundled by Zig 0.16.0, including musl and cloudlibc portions and
Zig runtime code. Upstream license alternatives and complete component notices
are retained in licenses/wasi-libc/ and licenses/zig/LICENSE. The C fixture is
in the source checkout, not the ordinary product bundle. The Zig Wasm examples
are built without -lc; their WASI target alone does not imply wasi-libc linkage.

LLVM libunwind:
Linux builds explicitly link Zig 0.16.0's bundled LLVM unwinder. Its complete
license, including LLVM exceptions and retained legacy notices, is in
licenses/llvm-libunwind/LICENSE.TXT.

Unicode/Python-derived property data:
loops/workspace-check/printable.zig and its compiled module contain Unicode
15.0.0 printability/whitespace data extracted using Python 3.12.3. fh transformed
the property results into contiguous nonprintable ranges and a whitespace set
represented as Zig source. Complete Unicode and pinned Python license texts
are in licenses/unicode/LICENSE and licenses/python/LICENSE. Python is an
authoring provenance source; it is not required for running this module.

License source paths and versions are documented in licenses/README.md.
The new standalone increment-source, increment-wasm and workspace-check Loop
packages also carry local LICENSE/NOTICE files and applicable complete licenses.

The macOS arm64 binary notice set retains all 235 packages in the resolved
Wasmtime C API normal/build dependency graph, including native ring and Zstandard
code and generated data. Build tools and optional source are included
conservatively; their inclusion does not assert that all their code is linked.
Zstandard uses its BSD-3-Clause alternative. Rust 1.97.0 standard-library and
compiler-builtins notices are retained under licenses/wasmtime/rust-1.97.0/.
See licenses/wasmtime/README.md for verified artifact and toolchain provenance.
